1. From (1) we deduce that for each fixed \(x\) the term \(x*y\) is independent of \(y\); thus there exists a function \(d:M\to M\) with \(x*y=d(x)\) for all \(y\).  
2. Substituting this into (1) gives \(d(x)=d(z*z)\) for all \(x,z\).  
3. Fix any \(z_0\). Then \(d(x)=d(z_0*z_0)\) for every \(x\);

